From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:42:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] libcamera: Add the Samsung S5K3J1 and S5KGM5 sensors

The S5K3J1 and S5KGM5 are the front and 5x telephoto cameras of the
Google Pixel 7 Pro, captured through the gs201 CSIS receiver and the
simple pipeline handler with the software ISP, as its main camera.

Add their camera sensor helpers: a black level of 64 at 10 bits and the
linear analogue gain of Samsung's sensors, code / 32 (0x20 is 1x). Add
their sensor properties: the unit cells of 1.22 um and 0.7 um the
phone's maker gives for these cameras, and two-frame control delays. The
test pattern numbering is not known, so no test pattern modes are
listed.

Add uncalibrated tuning files for the simple IPA: the identity colour
matrix so the saturation default applies, contrast 1.2 and saturation
1.1 as on the main camera, and autofocus on the telephoto's lens with
the main camera's step counts. The front camera has fixed focus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
